[{:db/id "q-38133/selection/d0ab94490dee12664d2f70471811316d5faf74c9c2c3f6dde546976ea292b76b" :answer/id #uuid "f7313f7a-b58a-581d-8b88-6ace41c36b14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38133/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer/id #uuid "e14a0e64-5cb8-5161-9283-7cdbc438df70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38133/selection/c357e6862530faa72ca0d68ad19a73c1e529aca9aa9b841a1f3dc13ec0b25f13" :answer/id #uuid "5c657196-04d0-5b2a-800d-a9c23cfdede3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi +4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38133/selection/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8" :answer/id #uuid "0a97a54a-fa79-53e7-838b-ca93fc0cf2f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38133/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" :answer/id #uuid "2eaad03e-529a-52c6-909e-f109880976f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38133/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d84eefc-a3a7-5e23-a25b-2fec9b265db9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-38133/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" :answer-field/choices ["q-38133/selection/d0ab94490dee12664d2f70471811316d5faf74c9c2c3f6dde546976ea292b76b" "q-38133/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" "q-38133/selection/c357e6862530faa72ca0d68ad19a73c1e529aca9aa9b841a1f3dc13ec0b25f13" "q-38133/selection/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8" "q-38133/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-38133" :question/id #uuid "bd8c290c-46b0-546e-b105-a7371cbafeab" :question/math-academy-id "q-38133" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta =$" :question/worked-solution "First, we integrate with respect to $r,$ treating $\\theta $ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{[\\frac{{r}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\frac{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}}{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}2{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate with respect to $\\theta :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}2{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={[\\theta +\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )]}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-38133/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bc5322f-ed04-53d2-8ce6-20ec58f73a5e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38133"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83955/selection/ae2d843630a4279d6fa3a77eaebfd22a5e2ff6b93621e00fdb2722be2439080e" :answer/id #uuid "cff20bea-7439-522f-bd59-fcd12d27d5d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83955/selection/908379ca21e57297ac624cadb43b55225dcf5cb966a4b17a727a1272c0da5b6d" :answer/id #uuid "6f68930e-0b47-5542-af81-e3a94b899b5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83955/selection/c57800a73636eb226ee0090d14e712c661a1bd711b14e78a277fc9be1683a0d1" :answer/id #uuid "e98fa51f-6a62-5c8d-84df-226873f293c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83955/selection/80d3ec14ef3d866db5d777f59681faf8587759cc17177a9d0f9f57fcbafe6ac4" :answer/id #uuid "a79d912a-f0a9-54d0-a0b2-43fc4aca87b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83955/selection/eda7935adb298c8a74838fc7189ccadb245f7a868f347c1008d8277d1bf3ec9a" :answer/id #uuid "a4e9eba4-c286-5817-972f-9758ee803cb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83955/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "07a72c4f-3304-568e-a551-c9fb31d124be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83955/selection/80d3ec14ef3d866db5d777f59681faf8587759cc17177a9d0f9f57fcbafe6ac4" :answer-field/choices ["q-83955/selection/ae2d843630a4279d6fa3a77eaebfd22a5e2ff6b93621e00fdb2722be2439080e" "q-83955/selection/908379ca21e57297ac624cadb43b55225dcf5cb966a4b17a727a1272c0da5b6d" "q-83955/selection/c57800a73636eb226ee0090d14e712c661a1bd711b14e78a277fc9be1683a0d1" "q-83955/selection/80d3ec14ef3d866db5d777f59681faf8587759cc17177a9d0f9f57fcbafe6ac4" "q-83955/selection/eda7935adb298c8a74838fc7189ccadb245f7a868f347c1008d8277d1bf3ec9a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83955" :question/id #uuid "1b9a1961-cfec-5ea0-aa17-358f76216410" :question/math-academy-id "q-83955" :question/problem "If $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{(y-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}\\le \\frac{1}{4},\\,x\\le 0},$ then ${∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to change the coordinate system from Cartesian coordinates to polar coordinates. To do this, we will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067931/assets/32c4bf490df51121ddf1575df8211033185d392fd5b08519971723b820da191f.png)\n\nNotice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $\\frac{1}{2}$ centered at $(0,\\frac{1}{2}).$ \n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the ${x}^{2}+{(y-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{(y-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ (r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta -r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{4} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )-r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ {r}^{2}-r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ r(r-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire semicircle, we must have $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits for $r$ and $\\theta .$ First of all, $r$ can vary from $r=0$ (at the origin) to $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ (at the boundary of the region): \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067931/assets/b1e2eac0041d0b0cb802561b3fb83fd8fab1b940cb6c42f698879837c06cbff0.png)\n\nSecondly, $\\theta $ can vary between $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (the positive $y$-axis) and $\\theta =\\pi $ (the negative $x$-axis):\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067931/assets/193601785ff94605d12b91b7cab1e7390af532ba1912530bd8d3f492324e2788.png)\n\nSo, in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}((r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2})\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{3}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-83955/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de1091c5-d81a-565f-a281-b2fb0d00c973"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83955"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83970/selection/8fcc78f3f3f1d133761c797b9998aacaab6a4545f0fcc24406e30f17b6d44d42" :answer/id #uuid "68d17e28-6492-5229-aaee-4302b188b3e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83970/selection/19d9562aa92245b981d7f813fef149c67d81b0ed7a06e1a8e89c24da645be73a" :answer/id #uuid "609a2895-a79e-516a-9893-127b9904b94f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi \\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83970/selection/21ca94e50fb993c606e1c9bfb21af6c1199b4dd049b4abbe6a37181e30b23b1e" :answer/id #uuid "bbd33aed-f9c6-5292-b4ef-01f954584970" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi \\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83970/selection/5e542eed8f462585c79e39910b2c34ef465e22c833f24ec3a22005b86e477a3f" :answer/id #uuid "08fdce84-3d28-5b2d-a3b7-6a87f663b77a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83970/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "a4317ef3-816f-5a45-a27f-0d7ae893de3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83970/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e673c351-c42f-5bfc-ade1-34e17eb7be97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83970/selection/19d9562aa92245b981d7f813fef149c67d81b0ed7a06e1a8e89c24da645be73a" :answer-field/choices ["q-83970/selection/8fcc78f3f3f1d133761c797b9998aacaab6a4545f0fcc24406e30f17b6d44d42" "q-83970/selection/19d9562aa92245b981d7f813fef149c67d81b0ed7a06e1a8e89c24da645be73a" "q-83970/selection/21ca94e50fb993c606e1c9bfb21af6c1199b4dd049b4abbe6a37181e30b23b1e" "q-83970/selection/5e542eed8f462585c79e39910b2c34ef465e22c833f24ec3a22005b86e477a3f" "q-83970/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83970" :question/id #uuid "0d3937fa-c397-5c82-8e5c-164ecad0379b" :question/math-academy-id "q-83970" :question/problem "Integrate the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}$ over the portion of the disk of radius $1$ centered at the origin, where $x\\le 0$ and $y\\le 0.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067931/assets/e4275e74a45deb22c0ed22546772e33fbd5caeb89a4036b1a2f4870e8ecf67a1.png)\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 1,\\,\\pi \\le \\theta \\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{2}{(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+1}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2r}{{r}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡({r}^{2}+1)]_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2[\\theta ]_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi \\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-83970/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b97f75d-c784-5f3a-984d-f9a5fdf21d61"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83970"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161052/selection/11ecf647e206aab75310adfa1adb57cf126cfa081988890c415771e6ab8bc0f3" :answer/id #uuid "e62f01e1-fa78-5188-a518-dcd46fb2382b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18+2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161052/selection/01bbf8ebd5069470431f8452e98a426e151975cb8793ee4f306144a87060a9a3" :answer/id #uuid "87171f87-1c34-5563-95f5-41dcd6eba908" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161052/selection/3fe0c2782ef9d49a7200cf08ec6a2381610c8be6c4d087640d3d1aa242e684c3" :answer/id #uuid "ebf2ff55-b81f-5358-8ef0-6929c218400f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "81\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161052/selection/2ebacc6a8ab5641abfb2b79350ccf93dce464349b384bff647adff549e523718" :answer/id #uuid "b8b3a64b-2cc9-5891-8a47-13b2fd86ad91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9+4\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161052/selection/90db7e50123f93e0e45998c4ad0bb485a30665aa29f0b12dde8b1840a9ab5183" :answer/id #uuid "e55f6f64-7e78-5a6e-a7bf-6d4d57d69a13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161052/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "67b6c25a-4750-56e9-a4a0-95464fd6b14d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161052/selection/3fe0c2782ef9d49a7200cf08ec6a2381610c8be6c4d087640d3d1aa242e684c3" :answer-field/choices ["q-161052/selection/11ecf647e206aab75310adfa1adb57cf126cfa081988890c415771e6ab8bc0f3" "q-161052/selection/01bbf8ebd5069470431f8452e98a426e151975cb8793ee4f306144a87060a9a3" "q-161052/selection/3fe0c2782ef9d49a7200cf08ec6a2381610c8be6c4d087640d3d1aa242e684c3" "q-161052/selection/2ebacc6a8ab5641abfb2b79350ccf93dce464349b384bff647adff549e523718" "q-161052/selection/90db7e50123f93e0e45998c4ad0bb485a30665aa29f0b12dde8b1840a9ab5183"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161052" :question/id #uuid "2686fcc3-f583-5dd7-b59b-47c6ab685620" :question/math-academy-id "q-161052" :question/problem "Integrate the function $f(x,y)=4{y}^{2}$ over the disk of radius $3$ centered at the origin." :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067931/assets/0a1de805051eff4ea82b4eefb7bb113c724b3d4e7304704831b6294ee4e4d674.png)\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 3,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}4{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}4(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3}4{r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{3}4{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,{[{r}^{4}]}_{0}^{3}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta (81-0)\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =81{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =81{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}{[\\theta -\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}[(2\\pi -0)-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =81\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161052/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b97f75d-c784-5f3a-984d-f9a5fdf21d61"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161052"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161065/selection/047c91f587561929c9905168f2f74415b3550257b36273887b109cc821487984" :answer/id #uuid "d954d846-c533-551a-a82f-65f751f2e734" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161065/selection/770b3162971c9eef74ad4f5d06dce472953bebbbc276561cb68b1749a2f64356" :answer/id #uuid "e8b14a46-949b-50e7-93d9-24aef2229e35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161065/selection/862a3afbb01719f7aec18f7bf18173e70064fe338ec0310ebb2f6be765664240" :answer/id #uuid "fa9b2736-8f14-51d7-9790-3ce6a610b82e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161065/selection/f29b744e22e316995d38c558f3f3f2d1ab8ebff2a8e23e4dac01802391ebd073" :answer/id #uuid "305f601d-a355-5355-8e31-2a43aa1a2b71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161065/selection/5c3862eeb5413baf6d5792b889d93f76afb5f8d7b95036b524df9dc8ab4a73fd" :answer/id #uuid "7ba221ec-f275-5c06-8a6c-cf7341a30dda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161065/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dcc08679-7f6a-5262-8a25-a6b96bf12b00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161065/selection/047c91f587561929c9905168f2f74415b3550257b36273887b109cc821487984" :answer-field/choices ["q-161065/selection/047c91f587561929c9905168f2f74415b3550257b36273887b109cc821487984" "q-161065/selection/770b3162971c9eef74ad4f5d06dce472953bebbbc276561cb68b1749a2f64356" "q-161065/selection/862a3afbb01719f7aec18f7bf18173e70064fe338ec0310ebb2f6be765664240" "q-161065/selection/f29b744e22e316995d38c558f3f3f2d1ab8ebff2a8e23e4dac01802391ebd073" "q-161065/selection/5c3862eeb5413baf6d5792b889d93f76afb5f8d7b95036b524df9dc8ab4a73fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161065" :question/id #uuid "a7b778e2-1e49-5fc9-b2a9-e6236a05633d" :question/math-academy-id "q-161065" :question/problem "If $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2}\\le 1},$ then ${∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to change the coordinate system from Cartesian coordinates to polar coordinates. To do this, we will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA={∬}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067931/assets/f0417011f46d3860b7de86fe652a7d80dd9787cb05c2057601b41c17e0c2b423.png)\n\nNotice that the region $D$ represents the disk of radius $1$ centered at $(0,1).$\n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the ${x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=1$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & =1 \\\\ {(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -1)}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta -2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1 & =1 \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )-2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ {r}^{2}-2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ r(r-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire circle, we must have $r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits for $r$ and $\\theta .$ First of all, $r$ can vary from $r=0$ (at the origin) to $r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ (at the boundary of the region): \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067931/assets/3f4bb1428a6cc9b7e191e1904636d654145d9a1f2fb1dd40843d8cd878194772.png)\n\nSecondly, $\\theta $ can vary between $\\theta =0$ (the positive $x$-axis) and $\\theta =\\pi $ (the negative $x$-axis):\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067931/assets/d6f4e054767650cd2a3d348aee8210af421e2df21792d79f42c5a58b5f4e82e6.png)\n\nSo, in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161065/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de1091c5-d81a-565f-a281-b2fb0d00c973"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161065"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
